================================================================================
  10. Comparison Against EnergyPlus Fourier Method
================================================================================
  EnergyPlus uses a 9-term Fourier series for declination/EOT (Threlkeld/ASHRAE).
  HARES uses a 7-term Spencer (1971) series — a widely-cited but simpler model.
  Typical Spencer altitude error: up to ~0.25° (this verification confirms).
  EnergyPlus accuracy is comparable: ~0.1-0.5° for hourly solar angles.
  Both are acceptable for building energy simulation (typical tolerance: ≤0.5°).

